Usage: agent-deck session focus [--remote <name>] <id> [--attach] [--json]

Signal the running agent-deck TUI (same profile) to reveal and
select the session with the given instance id on its next refresh.
With --attach, the TUI opens/attaches the session (as if you
pressed Enter on it) instead of only moving the cursor.
With --remote, <id> is a session on that remote: the TUI selects
its row under Remotes. Nothing local is created.

Options:
  -attach
    	Open/attach the session, not just select it
  -json
    	Output the written request as JSON
  -remote string
    	Focus a session of this configured remote (see 'agent-deck remote list'); <id> is the remote's own session id
